# Bridge daemon runtime cache. Written by the sidecar's BridgeDaemon whenever the Control Centre
# runs against this repository (first observed during PROJECTOS-V3-CONTROL-CENTRE-INTEGRATION1A).
# Generated state, never governance evidence — the governed records live in .projectops/phases/.
.projectops/bridge/
# Generated draft proposals. A draft is regenerable output bound to a HEAD that moves, and against
# this repository one run produced 4.7MB of conflict detail. The owner's OBJECTIVE record — the
# durable intent — is tracked; the derived draft body is not.
.projectops/drafts/

# Local machine configuration for the bridge daemon: absolute watch roots, machine-specific.
# The desktop E2E run generates it; it must never be committed.
projectos/control-center/bridge.config.json

# Zero-relay continuity: TRANSIENT runtime state only. The ledger, the checkpoint and the
# continuation record ARE evidence and are tracked; these three are not. The ownership lock holds a
# live pid and is meaningless in another checkout, the owner control file is a standing local
# instruction rather than a record of what happened, and the brief is an input the supervisor
# regenerates on every run. Committing them would be residue that a later handoff has to reconcile.
.projectops/continuity/ownership.lock.json
.projectops/continuity/owner-control.json
.projectops/continuity/*.brief.json

# Which project the desktop Control Centre currently has selected. Local runtime state written by
# the app on this machine -- not a governance record, and not the same on any two installs.
/selected-project.json

# The closure WAIT record: which decision bytes were presented to the owner, in THIS checkout.
# Transient and local, exactly like the continuity brief above. It is a NARROWING record — losing it
# makes `closure resume` refuse, never proceed — so it is never authority and never evidence.
#
# AND IT MUST NOT BE TRACKED, for a mechanical reason. G4-13 requires a clean working tree at the
# closure decision point. A wait written between the ask and the owner's commit would sit untracked
# in `git status --porcelain`, so the record that the phase is waiting for closure would itself
# refuse that closure. The DECISION it points at is tracked, committed by the owner, and is the thing
# that actually counts.
.projectops/closure/waits/
